      "statement": "The 16-label list refers to the model file's field basis: F, P and R are charge-degenerate, so a U(5) rotation of the five X = 1 sixteens (F x3, P, R) can move couplings between declared and undeclared labels. The truncation is basis independent: the undeclared couplings span 24 complex = 48 real generation-expanded dimensions, while the only gauge-covariant (SO(10) x U(1)_X), linear, kinetic-term-preserving field-redefinition factor that mixes distinct multiplets is that U(5) (25 real dimensions); every other factor rotates the generations of a single multiplet or rephases it and maps the declared coupling space to itself. The orbit of the declared couplings (100 real dimensions) under all field redefinitions therefore has real dimension at most 100 + 25 = 125 < 148, the real dimension of all 26 couplings, so a generic Lagrangian with all 26 couplings is not field-redefinition-equivalent to a declared one",
